[[:db/cas 17592186120421 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 11\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.$" "Which of the following matrices are upper triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186440235 :answer-field/key "A" "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 7 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/ensure 17592186440235 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186440236 :answer-field/key "B" "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 3 \\\\ 5 & 7 & 11\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/ensure 17592186440236 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186440237 :answer-field/key "C" "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/ensure 17592186440237 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186120421 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186120422 :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $A$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** ${A}^{T}$ is upper triangular" "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186120422 :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $A$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true. All the entries below the main diagonal of ${A}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only\"." "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **True.** All the entries above the main diagonal of $A$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **True.** All the entries below the main diagonal of ${A}^{T}$ are zeros:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular.\n- ${A}^{T}$ is upper triangular."] [:db/cas 17592186439180 :answer-field/key "I" "$A$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186439180 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186439181 :answer-field/key "II" "$A$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186439181 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186439182 :answer-field/key "III" "${A}^{T}$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186439182 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186120422 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186120426 :question/problem "Consider the matrix\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$.\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $A^{T} + A$ is upper triangular\n- **III.** $A$ is lower triangular" "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186120426 :question/worked-solution "A is neither upper nor lower triangular because both off-diagonal entries a12=1 and a21=-1 are nonzero. However A^T+A=diag(-6,2,10), so statement II is true." "$A$ is neither upper nor lower triangular because $a_{12}=1$ and $a_{21}=-1$ are both nonzero. However,\n\n$$\nA^{T}+A=\\begin{bmatrix}-6 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 10\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nis diagonal, so $A^{T}+A$ is upper triangular."] [:db/cas 17592186440238 :answer-field/key "I" "$A$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186440238 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186440239 :answer-field/key "II" "$A^{T} + A$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186440239 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186440240 :answer-field/key "III" "$A$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186440240 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186120426 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186262604 :question/problem "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$" "Which of the following matrices are lower triangular matrices?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186438896 :answer-field/key "A" "$A=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/ensure 17592186438896 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438897 :answer-field/key "B" "$B=\\begin{bmatrix}5 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/ensure 17592186438897 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438898 :answer-field/key "C" "$C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}$"] [:db/ensure 17592186438898 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186262604 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186262616 :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $B$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular" "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186262616 :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since the result of $B-{B}^{T}$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB-{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $B$ is upper triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries below the main diagonal equal to zero:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is lower triangular: **False.** This fails because $B$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 4 & 5 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 2\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B-{B}^{T}$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because the result of $B-{B}^{T}$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB-{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & 5 \\\\ 0 & -1 & -5 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $B$ is upper triangular."] [:db/cas 17592186438899 :answer-field/key "I" "$B$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438899 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438900 