atrix}5 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $C$ is upper triangular.\n- $C$ is lower triangular.\n- ${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular."] [:db/cas 17592186438902 :answer-field/key "I" "$C$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438902 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438903 :answer-field/key "II" "$C$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438903 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438904 :answer-field/key "III" "${C}^{T}$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438904 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186262617 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186262618 :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$B=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $B$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** ${B}^{T}$ is lower triangular" "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186262618 :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true. All the entries above the main diagonal of $B$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since $B$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only\"." "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $B$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because $B$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $B$ is lower triangular: **True.** All the entries above the main diagonal of $B$ are zeros:\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 4 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${B}^{T}$ is lower triangular: **False.** It has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{B}^{T}=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 4 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 5\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $B$ is lower triangular."] [:db/cas 17592186438905 :answer-field/key "I" "$B$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438905 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438906 :answer-field/key "II" "$B$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438906 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438907 :answer-field/key "III" "${B}^{T}$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438907 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186262618 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186269146 :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n\n- **II.** $A$ is lower triangular\n\n- **III.** ${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular" "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186269146 :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is true, since the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries above the main diagonal equal to zero: \n\n$$\n{A}^{T}+A=\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I, II, and III\"." "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries below the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular: **True.** This holds because the result of $A+{A}^{T}$ has all the entries above the main diagonal equal to zero: \n\n$$\n{A}^{T}+A=\\begin{bmatrix}16 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 6\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular.\n- $A$ is lower triangular.\n- ${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular."] [:db/cas 17592186438986 :answer-field/key "I" "$A$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438986 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438987 :answer-field/key "II" "$A$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438987 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186438988 :answer-field/key "III" "${A}^{T}+A$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186438988 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186269146 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186326929 :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is lower triangular\n- **II.** ${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $A$ is upper triangular" "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply."] [:db/cas 17592186326929 :question/worked-solution "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- Statement I is true, since all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false, since the result of ${A}^{T}-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}-A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- Statement III is false, since $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\"." "Let's analyze each statement in turn.\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular: **True.** This holds because all the entries above the main diagonal are zeros:\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- ${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular: **False.** This fails because the result of ${A}^{T}-A$ has non-zero entries above the main diagonal:\n\n$$\n{A}^{T}-A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n- $A$ is upper triangular: **False.** This fails because $A$ has non-zero entries below the main diagonal\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}7 & 0 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nThe true statements are:\n\n- $A$ is lower triangular."] [:db/cas 17592186439183 :answer-field/key "I" "$A$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186439183 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186439184 :answer-field/key "II" "${A}^{T}-A$ is lower triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186439184 :answer-field/validate] [:db/cas 17592186439185 :answer-field/key "III" "$A$ is upper triangular."] [:db/ensure 17592186439185 :answer-field/validate] [:db/ensure 17592186326929 :question/validate] [:db/cas 17592186335970 :question/problem "Consider the matrix \n$A=\\begin{bmatrix}0 & -2 & -7 \\\\ 2 & -1 & 8 \\\\ 7 & -8 & 1\\end{bmatrix}.$\nWhich of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $A$ is upper triangular\n- **II.** $A$ is lower triangular\n- **III.** $A+{A}^{T}$ is upper triangular" "Consider the matrix\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmat